1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,450
What if the internet went down for one whole day?

2
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:05,500
It already happened.

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:09,220
In twenty twenty-two, twelve million Canadians lost their phones and internet.

4
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:11,230
Debit cards stopped working across the country.

5
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,190
Now imagine the whole world.

6
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:14,410
You wake up.

7
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,300
No messages. No news.

8
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,090
No maps.

9
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,310
You tap your card.

10
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:19,940
Declined. Cash only.

11
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:23,760
Offices freeze. Email, video calls, cloud files: gone.

12
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,190
Airports go into chaos.

13
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:30,210
In twenty twenty-four, one bad software update cancelled over five thousand flights in a single day.

14
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:32,000
No deliveries. No rides.

15
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:32,790
No streaming.

16
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:35,310
And the bill for one day?

17
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:37,810
About forty-three billion dollars.

18
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:39,850
So, could you survive a day offline?

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,850
Comment below.
